00:38:17.080 --> 00:38:20.665
An anonymous question
that came in was,

00:38:21.490 --> 00:38:22.870
if only or--

00:38:22.870 --> 00:38:23.410
what is this?

00:38:23.410 --> 00:38:26.620
If only there was a good
way to share these data science endpoints,

00:38:26.620 --> 00:38:30.010
do you have any advice on
deploying and managing these

00:38:30.010 --> 00:38:30.880
kinds of outputs?

00:38:31.450 --> 00:38:37.420
- Yeah. So I think that
it is really important to find

00:38:38.110 --> 00:38:40.060
an easy way to

00:38:42.430 --> 00:38:44.084
do this in a--

00:38:46.354 --> 00:38:49.570
like be able to have an MVP,
to be able to have a demo,

00:38:50.200 --> 00:38:53.170
and then you can work
from there. So if you--

00:38:53.170 --> 00:38:57.460
for those of you who are
customers or having trying to

00:38:57.460 --> 00:38:58.840
make a argument around it,

00:38:58.840 --> 00:39:00.850
like that is exactly
what Connect does.

00:39:00.850 --> 00:39:06.330
Like Connect is a way that you
as a data scientist can deploy something

00:39:07.450 --> 00:39:10.390
with one function,
with one button click.

00:39:10.390 --> 00:39:14.710
Like it really lets you have a playground.

00:39:14.710 --> 00:39:16.000
And then depending on the--

00:39:16.840 --> 00:39:20.110
it really reduces the barrier
to that first like, ah,

00:39:20.110 --> 00:39:22.295
I am serving an API.
Like here it is.

00:39:23.550 --> 00:39:27.305
If you are in a situation
where that's not reasonable for your org,

00:39:27.980 --> 00:39:29.930
I think that the--

00:39:29.930 --> 00:39:32.510
then you are in a situation
where you need to have a

00:39:32.510 --> 00:39:35.240
conversation with your
organization is like well since

00:39:35.240 --> 00:39:37.625
we don't have a
tool that does this,

00:39:38.640 --> 00:39:42.650
then you are asking me to
gain some of that skill. Like are

00:39:42.650 --> 00:39:45.440
you making space for that? Is
that what we're going to do?

00:39:45.440 --> 00:39:48.530
Because if it's not like
a product kind of thing,

00:39:48.530 --> 00:39:51.000
like Connect that really
is built for you as

00:39:51.740 --> 00:39:54.620
like you are the
one it is built for,

00:39:54.620 --> 00:39:57.440
like you as a data scientist
to be able to deploy an API,

00:39:57.440 --> 00:40:00.410
publish an app, all these kinds
of things. Then you're like OK,

00:40:00.410 --> 00:40:02.030
then I need to
be able to make--

00:40:02.030 --> 00:40:05.120
then you need like the
org needs to acknowledge

00:40:06.140 --> 00:40:08.730
that you're asking me to
gain some of those skills.

00:40:08.730 --> 00:40:09.830
And so I think--

