00:41:24.380 --> 00:41:26.690
There's a lot of ways
to answer that question.

00:41:26.690 --> 00:41:29.960
And some of them are quite easy
and built for you as a data

00:41:29.960 --> 00:41:33.090
science user persona.
And some of them mean,

00:41:33.090 --> 00:41:36.680
you really do have to
start going into those more ops-y

00:41:36.680 --> 00:41:40.180
areas. I will say, if you
are a person that combines

00:41:41.000 --> 00:41:42.230
like statistical know-how

00:41:43.010 --> 00:41:45.695
with like ops-y know-how,

00:41:46.490 --> 00:41:52.400
that's killer, career-wise. So I
mean, go for it. If you're

00:41:52.400 --> 00:41:53.810
interested and

00:41:55.160 --> 00:41:57.410
you have a little bit of
the space to start gaining those

00:41:57.410 --> 00:42:00.140
skills like that,
that's fantastic.

00:42:01.040 --> 00:42:03.230
Those are people who's--

00:42:03.230 --> 00:42:06.770
like that set of skills
combo of skills is like super

00:42:06.770 --> 00:42:09.740
valuable in the market.
When you hear about, oh,

00:42:09.740 --> 00:42:10.940
data scientists. Oh.

00:42:12.110 --> 00:42:15.080
I'm so annoyed. It's like
data scientists never ship,

00:42:15.080 --> 00:42:18.080
data scientists have
terrible software engineering practices

00:42:18.080 --> 00:42:21.620
like the coding practices. So
if you are someone who's like

00:42:21.620 --> 00:42:23.120
no, no. I can do that.

00:42:23.120 --> 00:42:26.480
I know how to do that. I
can learn. I have learned X.

00:42:26.480 --> 00:42:27.770
I'm in the process
of learning Y.

00:42:27.770 --> 00:42:28.827
Like that's

00:42:30.110 --> 00:42:31.700
wonderful for your career.

00:42:31.700 --> 00:42:34.560
So that's like a look
on the bright side,

00:42:34.560 --> 00:42:37.700
kind of like silver lining
kind of situation, if

00:42:38.870 --> 00:42:39.950
that is true for you.

00:42:41.590 --> 00:42:42.490
- Thank you.

