00:54:19.420 --> 00:54:21.280
And so they already
had kind of this ethos.

00:54:21.280 --> 00:54:23.320
And so when I showed
up, and I'm like, oh.

00:54:23.980 --> 00:54:25.540
We're going to
do this and this.

00:54:25.540 --> 00:54:26.040
And

00:54:27.670 --> 00:54:31.270
like I want to open source
this piece. And they're like, yeah,

00:54:31.270 --> 00:54:33.715
sure. So that's the
kind of situation where

00:54:34.780 --> 00:54:36.280
people already have buy in.

00:54:36.280 --> 00:54:39.550
But if you work in like health
care or you work in finance or

00:54:39.550 --> 00:54:41.125
you work in something
that has higher

00:54:44.380 --> 00:54:45.850
constraints around

00:54:47.700 --> 00:54:51.660
like data privacy then a
tech company where everything is

00:54:51.660 --> 00:54:52.590
kind of public anyway.

00:54:52.590 --> 00:54:53.730
It's like all on Stack

00:54:54.690 --> 00:54:55.590
Overflow it's like--

00:54:55.590 --> 00:54:56.090
there

00:54:56.730 --> 00:54:59.310
is user data that you don't
want linked but so much of it

00:54:59.310 --> 00:55:01.770
is like, there's a public
kind of ethos. That was different.

00:55:01.770 --> 00:55:03.720
If you don't work
in that, I think--

00:55:04.800 --> 00:55:07.320
I think the thing
to do is to clearly

00:55:08.760 --> 00:55:13.680
lay out why they should do
it at all. And I think--

00:55:13.680 --> 00:55:17.100
I think there's like why
should they let you--

00:55:17.100 --> 00:55:20.325
like let you spend time on
that? And I think one is--

00:55:22.170 --> 00:55:23.700
one is that--

00:55:23.700 --> 00:55:26.010
like depending,
and in this market,

00:55:26.010 --> 00:55:27.690
maybe this is not so
compelling. But like for

00:55:27.690 --> 00:55:31.470
recruiting, like if you are
in an org and you're like--

00:55:32.920 --> 00:55:37.620
we work in like a field that's
viewed as a little stuffy or boring.

00:55:37.620 --> 00:55:40.290
But you're like, no.
We can show people that

00:55:41.280 --> 00:55:43.380
the kind of work
we do by having

00:55:44.220 --> 00:55:47.170
an open source library or to--

00:55:47.170 --> 00:55:48.220
and you can say like,

00:55:48.220 --> 00:55:50.950
it can be used as a recruiting
tool to show people the kind of

00:55:50.950 --> 00:55:53.530
tools they'll be using
with, the kind of way--

00:55:53.530 --> 00:55:55.825
So there's like
recruiting. There is--

00:55:57.490 --> 00:55:58.420
like I know,

00:55:58.420 --> 00:56:01.060
pharma has just gone through
like a big kind of like--

00:56:01.060 --> 00:56:04.390
is it like, if we all band
together and make these tools,

00:56:05.230 --> 00:56:09.220
we can use them then in
our compliance like how we need to

00:56:09.220 --> 00:56:10.460
report kinds of things.

00:56:10.460 --> 00:56:12.190
- That's exactly what
I would love to do to.

00:56:12.190 --> 00:56:12.690
- Yeah.

00:56:14.740 --> 00:56:14.965
-

00:56:14.965 --> 00:56:17.890
Get all the brains together
in the health care insurance space

00:56:17.890 --> 00:56:19.510
for the greater good.

00:56:19.510 --> 00:56:20.010
- Yeah.

00:56:20.560 --> 00:56:21.970
Yeah. Yeah. Yeah. So I think--

00:56:21.970 --> 00:56:22.470
I think

00:56:25.120 --> 00:56:26.792
that there has to be a

00:56:28.210 --> 00:56:29.130
compelling

00:56:29.890 --> 00:56:32.446
case made. And then also, how

00:56:34.390 --> 00:56:35.990
are you going to make sure--

00:56:36.730 --> 00:56:37.230
what

00:56:39.310 --> 00:56:40.990
processes are going
to be in place?

00:56:40.990 --> 00:56:44.980
So there are reasonable
concerns about data privacy are

00:56:44.980 --> 00:56:46.915
addressed. So I think--

00:56:47.440 --> 00:56:49.960
it's definitely tougher
when you are in--

00:56:49.960 --> 00:56:51.630
when you are in an

00:56:52.630 --> 00:56:55.960
industry that has
high compliance standards.

00:56:56.680 --> 00:57:00.118
But I do think the
pharma example is one of why--

00:57:01.450 --> 00:57:02.860
like how it can work out,

00:57:02.860 --> 00:57:05.500
how it can work out
to make things better actually overall

00:57:05.500 --> 00:57:08.110
for everyone. I mean,
those people are all like

00:57:08.110 --> 00:57:10.300
competitors. I'm
always so amazed.

00:57:10.300 --> 00:57:13.330
I'm always so amazed at
how they collaborate.

00:57:13.330 --> 00:57:14.170
It's pretty cool.

